; A CONFORMANCE WITNESS, not a useful program. It exists to pin one normative
; rule in §7 that would otherwise rest on prose alone:
;
;   when eager body-registration of a NON-TOTAL callee reaches an operator
;   EXCLUDED from translation, no direct-attempt script is emitted for the
;   property whose goal triggered it, and its line is ABSENT from
;   prove/scripts.txt.
;
; That rule used to be witnessed by decimal `show`, which recurses on `n / 10`.
; #71 made Int `/` and `%` translatable, so `show-nat` now emits a script and
; proves — and the rule silently lost its only corpus witness. A rule pinned by
; nothing is a rule two kernels can quietly disagree about (see DIVERGENCES 83a
; for what that costs), so it is re-witnessed here with an exclusion that
; REMAINS excluded: partial application.
;
; Do not "simplify" this away. Each piece is load-bearing:
;   - apply2 has arity 2, so applying it to one argument is a partial
;     application — outside the provable fragment (§7.1).
;   - spin-partial is NON-TOTAL by construction (the x >= 0 branch never
;     descends), which is what makes its body eagerly registered rather than
;     merely asserted, and its body contains the partial application.
;   - excluded-witness.reaches-excluded-op references spin-partial, so the goal
;     drags that body in and hits the exclusion. Its sibling
;     independent-of-exclusion does NOT, and still emits a script — that
;     contrast is the point: suppression must be per-goal, not per-definition.
; The guard `(< x 0)` keeps the property TRUE and testable: spin-partial
; terminates on negatives, so the deterministic tester passes rather than
; fuelling out, and the definition records `tested` instead of falsified.

(defn apply2 [] [(a Int) (b Int)] Int
  (+ a b))

(defn spin-partial [] [(x Int)] (-> Int Int)
  (if (< x 0) (apply2 x) (spin-partial x)))

(defn excluded-witness [] [(x Int)] Int
  (+ x 1)
  (prop independent-of-exclusion [(x Int)]
    (== (excluded-witness x) (+ x 1)))
  (prop reaches-excluded-op [(x Int)]
    (if (< x 0) (== ((spin-partial x) 0) ((spin-partial x) 0)) true)))
